---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
---

<MainLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | NumanX Tools"
  description="How NumanX Tools handles your files, cookies, analytics, and the contact, feedback and newsletter forms, and the third-party services involved."
  keywords="privacy policy, numanx privacy, data protection, GDPR, cookies policy"
  canonical="https://toolshub.numanxstudio.com/privacy-policy/"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Privacy Policy', url: '/privacy-policy/' },
  ]}
>
  <main class="min-h-screen pt-16 pb-20 px-6 relative overflow-hidden">
    <div
      class="absolute top-[10%] right-[5%] w-[300px] h-[300px] rounded-full bg-amber-600/10 blur-[100px] pointer-events-none -z-10"
    >
    </div>
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <!-- Hero -->
      <section class="text-center mb-16 pt-8">
        <div
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-700/50 bg-zinc-900/80 text-tertiary text-xs font-semibold tracking-wider uppercase mb-8"
        >
          <svg
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="14"
            height="14"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            class="text-amber-400"
            ><rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="11" rx="2" ry="2"></rect><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"
            ></path></svg
          >
          Privacy &amp; Security
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-black tracking-tight leading-none">
          <span class="text-amber-400"
            >Privacy Policy</span
          >
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-tertiary text-sm">Last updated: November 2026</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-tertiary max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          The tools on this site run in your browser, so the files and text you put into them are not uploaded. Some
          other parts of the site do send data: analytics (only if you accept it), the contact, feedback and newsletter
          forms, and a few downloads from outside servers. This page explains each one.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Content -->
      <div class="space-y-8">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/40 p-6 md:p-8 shadow-xl">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">1. When You Visit the Site</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-tertiary leading-relaxed">
            The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Like any web host, Cloudflare receives your IP address and browser
            details when it delivers a page. You don&rsquo;t need an account to use any tool. Cloudflare&rsquo;s Web
            Analytics feature is switched on for this site, but the site&rsquo;s security settings currently block its
            script, so it does not run.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-tertiary leading-relaxed">
            Until you choose &ldquo;Accept all&rdquo; in the cookie banner, no analytics or advertising scripts load. A
            few features download code or data from outside servers, which receive a normal download request (your IP
            address and browser details) but not your files or text:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm text-tertiary">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&bull;</span><span
                ><strong class="text-secondary">Site search:</strong> loads the Fuse.js search library from cdn.jsdelivr.net
                when you search.</span
              >
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&bull;</span><span
                ><strong class="text-secondary">AI Background Remover:</strong> downloads its model files from IMG.LY&rsquo;s
                server (staticimgly.com). Your photo is processed on your device and is not sent.</span
              >
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&bull;</span><span
                ><strong class="text-secondary">Markdown to PDF:</strong> loads its Markdown, maths and diagram libraries
                from cdn.jsdelivr.net.</span
              >
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/40 p-6 md:p-8 shadow-xl">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">2. Tools and Your Files</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-tertiary leading-relaxed">
            The tools process your files and text in your browser using standard web features (such as Canvas, Web
            Workers and Web Crypto). Files you open in a tool are not uploaded to our servers or anyone else&rsquo;s. The
            AI Image Upscaler loads its model from this site; the AI Background Remover loads its model as described
            above.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/40 p-6 md:p-8 shadow-xl">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">3. Data Saved in Your Browser</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-tertiary leading-relaxed">
            Some features save data in your browser&rsquo;s local storage so it is still there next time. This data stays
            on your device and is not sent to us:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm text-tertiary">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&bull;</span><span
                >Drafts you type into some text tools, and the assistant chat history and name you give it</span
              >
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&bull;</span><span
                >Favourites, recently used tools, tool settings and your light/dark theme</span
              >
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&bull;</span><span>Your cookie choice</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-tertiary leading-relaxed">
            Generated passwords are kept in memory only and are gone when you close the page. You can delete everything
            else by clearing this site&rsquo;s data in your browser settings.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/40 p-6 md:p-8 shadow-xl">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">4. Cookies &amp; Analytics</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-tertiary leading-relaxed">
            The cookie banner offers &ldquo;Essential only&rdquo; or &ldquo;Accept all&rdquo;. Until you choose, analytics
            stays off.
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm text-tertiary">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&bull;</span><span
                ><strong class="text-secondary">Essential only:</strong> no analytics scripts load and no analytics cookies
                are set.</span
              >
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&bull;</span><span
                ><strong class="text-secondary">Accept all:</strong> your browser loads the Google Tag Manager and Google
                Analytics scripts from Google, which receives a normal download request (your IP address and browser
                details). When Google Analytics is collecting data, it sets cookies (such as <code>_ga</code>) holding a
                random ID for your browser, and sends Google the pages you visit and your device and browser details.
                The same events go to two Google Analytics properties that NumanX Tools uses (<code>G-64JVWY8F6W</code>
                and <code>G-SYQLJP44L7</code>), so each visit is counted in both. Google uses your IP address to estimate your approximate location (such as city or country); Google
                says it does not log or store the IP addresses of visitors from the EU, UK and Switzerland. We use this
                to see which tools people use.</span
              >
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&bull;</span><span
                ><strong class="text-secondary">Changing your mind:</strong> use &ldquo;Cookie Settings&rdquo; in the footer
                at any time and choose &ldquo;Essential only&rdquo;. When you withdraw consent, we stop sending subsequent
                analytics events to both Google Analytics properties on the current page and prevent analytics from
                loading on subsequent pages. The Google Analytics cookies set on this site are deleted at the same
                time.</span
              >
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/40 p-6 md:p-8 shadow-xl">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">5. Advertising, Links, Tips &amp; Sponsorship</h2>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-tertiary">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&bull;</span><span
                ><strong class="text-secondary">Advertising:</strong> the site does not run paid advertising or load any
                advertising network.</span
              >
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&bull;</span><span
                ><strong class="text-secondary">Product links:</strong> some pages link to other products (such as vidIQ,
                NordPass, Canva and Hostinger), shown with a &ldquo;Partner link&rdquo; label. We do not currently earn
                affiliate commissions from these links. They add a tag (<code>utm_source=numanx_tools</code>) that tells
                the other site you came from NumanX Tools.</span
              >
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&bull;</span><span
                ><strong class="text-secondary">Tips:</strong> some pages invite voluntary tips through payment apps. If
                you send one, the payment service handles your details under its own policy.</span
              >
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&bull;</span><span
                ><strong class="text-secondary">Sponsorship:</strong> some pages invite sponsorship enquiries by email.
                Emails you send us are kept in our inbox.</span
              >
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-tertiary leading-relaxed">
            Once you leave this site, the other site&rsquo;s own privacy policy applies.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/40 p-6 md:p-8 shadow-xl">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">6. Contact, Feedback &amp; Newsletter Forms</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-tertiary leading-relaxed">
            These forms are the only part of the site that sends personal details you type to a server. What you
            send:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm text-tertiary">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&bull;</span><span
                ><strong class="text-secondary">Contact form:</strong> your name, email address, topic and message. You get
                an automatic &ldquo;we got your message&rdquo; email.</span
              >
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&bull;</span><span
                ><strong class="text-secondary">Feedback form:</strong> your rating, message and the page you were on, plus
                your name and email if you give them. If you give an email, you get a thank-you email.</span
              >
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&bull;</span><span
                ><strong class="text-secondary">Newsletter:</strong> your email address. You are only subscribed after you
                click the link in the confirmation email, and every newsletter email has an unsubscribe link.</span
              >
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-tertiary leading-relaxed">
            Your submission goes to a Cloudflare Pages Function on this site, which passes it to a Google Apps Script.
            The script saves it as a row in a Google Sheet that we control and sends the emails through Gmail, so a copy
            also sits in our email. We use these details only to reply to you, act on your feedback or send the
            newsletter you asked for.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-tertiary leading-relaxed">
            <strong class="text-secondary">How long it is kept:</strong> we have not set a retention period, and
            submissions are not deleted automatically from the Google Sheet or our email. Cloudflare and Google may also
            keep their own records of the request under their own policies.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/40 p-6 md:p-8 shadow-xl">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">7. Your Rights</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-tertiary leading-relaxed">
            Depending on where you live, data protection laws may give you rights over your personal data, such as
            asking what we hold about you, or asking for it to be corrected or erased. To ask about your data, email us
            at the address below.
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm text-tertiary">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&bull;</span><span
                ><strong class="text-secondary">No Sale:</strong> We do not sell your personal information.</span
              >
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&bull;</span><span
                ><strong class="text-secondary">Right to Withdraw Consent:</strong> You can turn analytics off at any time
                with &ldquo;Cookie Settings&rdquo; in the footer.</span
              >
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&bull;</span><span
                ><strong class="text-secondary">Sharing:</strong> Personal details are handled by the services that run
                parts of the site for us, as described on this page: Cloudflare (hosting and the form function) and Google
                (Apps Script, Sheets and Gmail for forms, and Analytics if you accept it).</span
              >
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/40 p-6 md:p-8 shadow-xl">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">8. Third-Party Links</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-tertiary leading-relaxed">
            Our website may contain links to third-party websites. We are not responsible for the privacy practices of
            these external sites. We encourage you to review their privacy policies before engaging.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/40 p-6 md:p-8 shadow-xl">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">9. Children&rsquo;s Privacy</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-tertiary leading-relaxed">
            NumanX Tools is not aimed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their personal details. The
            tools do not ask for personal data.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/40 p-6 md:p-8 shadow-xl">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-tertiary leading-relaxed">
            We may update this privacy policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated
            revision date. We encourage you to review this policy periodically.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/40 p-6 md:p-8 shadow-xl">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">11. Contact Us</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-tertiary leading-relaxed">
            If you have any questions, concerns, or requests regarding this privacy policy, please contact us:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm text-tertiary">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&bull;</span><span
                >Email: <a
                  href="mailto:contact@numanxstudio.com"
                  class="text-amber-400 hover:text-amber-300 underline">contact@numanxstudio.com</a
                ></span
              >
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&bull;</span><span
                >Contact Form: <a href="/contact/" class="text-amber-400 hover:text-amber-300 underline"
                  >Visit our Contact page</a
                ></span
              >
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Trust Badges -->
      <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/40 p-4 text-center hover:border-zinc-700 transition-all duration-300">
          <div class="text-2xl mb-2">🔒</div>
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-secondary">HTTPS Only</p>
          <p class="text-[10px] text-dim mt-0.5">Encrypted connection</p>
        </div>
        <div
          class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/40 p-4 text-center hover:border-zinc-700 transition-all duration-300"
        >
          <div class="text-2xl mb-2">🛡️</div>
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-secondary">No File Uploads</p>
          <p class="text-[10px] text-dim mt-0.5">Tools run in your browser</p>
        </div>
        <div
          class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/40 p-4 text-center hover:border-zinc-700 transition-all duration-300"
        >
          <div class="text-2xl mb-2">🍪</div>
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-secondary">Analytics Opt-In</p>
          <p class="text-[10px] text-dim mt-0.5">Off until you accept</p>
        </div>
        <div
          class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/40 p-4 text-center hover:border-zinc-700 transition-all duration-300"
        >
          <div class="text-2xl mb-2">✅</div>
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-secondary">No Data Sold</p>
          <p class="text-[10px] text-dim mt-0.5">No paid ads</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- CTA -->
      <section class="mt-12 text-center">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/30 p-8 shadow-xl">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Questions About Privacy?</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-tertiary mt-2">We&rsquo;re here to help. Reach out anytime.</p>
          <a
            href="/contact/"
            class="inline-block mt-4 bg-amber-600 hover:bg-amber-700 text-accent-fg font-semibold text-sm px-6 py-3 rounded-xl transition-all duration-200"
          >
            Contact Us
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</MainLayout>
